> conj(-1)
conj((-1)) = -1
  check: equal numerically (-1, complex arithmetic)
> conj(i)
conj((i)) = -i
  check: equal numerically (-1i, complex arithmetic)
> conj(2+3i)
conj((2+3i)) = 2 - 3i
  check: equal numerically (2 - 3i, complex arithmetic)
> conj(-1+2i)
conj((-1+2i)) = -1 - 2i
  check: equal numerically (-1 - 2i, complex arithmetic)
> conj(conj(2+3i))
conj((conj(2+3i))) = 2 + 3i
  check: equal numerically (2 + 3i, complex arithmetic)
> re(conj(2+3i))
Re((conj(2+3i))) = 2
  check: equal numerically (2, complex arithmetic)
> im(conj(2+3i))
Im((conj(2+3i))) = -3
  check: equal numerically (-3, complex arithmetic)
> arg(conj(-1+i))
arg((conj(-1+i))) = -3pi/4
  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi
  check: equal numerically (-2.35619449, complex arithmetic)
> arg(conj(-1-i))
arg((conj(-1-i))) = 3pi/4
  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi
  check: equal numerically (2.35619449, complex arithmetic)
> modulus(-1)
|(-1)| = 1
  check: equal numerically (1, complex arithmetic)
> modulus(i)
|(i)| = 1
  check: equal numerically (1, complex arithmetic)
> modulus(3+4i)
|(3+4i)| = 5
  check: equal numerically (5, complex arithmetic)
> polar(-1)
(-1) = e^(i*pi)
  = cos(pi) + i*sin(pi)
  r = |z| = 1,  theta = arg z = pi
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (-1, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (-1, complex arithmetic)
> polar(-2)
(-2) = 2*e^(i*pi)
  = 2*(cos(pi) + i*sin(pi))
  r = |z| = 2,  theta = arg z = pi
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (-2, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (-2, complex arithmetic)
> polar(i)
(i) = e^(i*pi/2)
  = cos(pi/2) + i*sin(pi/2)
  r = |z| = 1,  theta = arg z = pi/2
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (1i, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (1i, complex arithmetic)
> polar(-i)
(-i) = e^(-i*pi/2)
  = cos(-pi/2) + i*sin(-pi/2)
  r = |z| = 1,  theta = arg z = -pi/2
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (-1i, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (-1i, complex arithmetic)
> polar(1+i)
(1+i) = sqrt(2)*e^(i*pi/4)
  = sqrt(2)*(cos(pi/4) + i*sin(pi/4))
  r = |z| = sqrt(2),  theta = arg z = pi/4
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (1 + 1i, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (1 + 1i, complex arithmetic)
> polar(-1-i)
(-1-i) = sqrt(2)*e^(-i*3pi/4)
  = sqrt(2)*(cos(-3pi/4) + i*sin(-3pi/4))
  r = |z| = sqrt(2),  theta = arg z = -3pi/4
  theta is the principal argument, -pi < theta <= pi
  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)
  check: equal numerically (-1 - 1i, complex arithmetic)
> re(z^2)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
Re((x + i*y)^2) = x^2 - y^2
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
> im(z^2)
  note: z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)
  note: z = x + iy (real and imaginary parts real)
  note: i is the imaginary unit; x, y are taken as real
Im((x + i*y)^2) = 2x*y
  check: equal at 64 of 64 sample points
